							</div>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=522.msg7609#msg7609"><img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=522.msg7609#msg7609">the streets code..</a></b>
									<div class="smalltext">&#171; <b> on:</b> December 06, 2006, 11:52:05 pm &#187;</div></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;">so me and mom were listening to g-code by geto boys in the car today when the discussion that unearthed this information happened....<br /><br />my mom (who comes from a long line of quakers) doesn&#039;t condone snitching except in cases where the prospective informant/testifier feels that society will benefit from the information they would provide, regardless of the law. for example, when my sister&#039;s school gave her and other students a choice between revealing names or being suspended after a bumpin&#039; party, my mom told her she&#039;d pull her out of school entirely before she&#039;d see her betray her friends under such petty circumstances.<br /><br />my own views are a little bit more extreme. i feel that if another party can solve a problem more effectively/fairly than the institution requesting my testimony, i should withhold it. for example, if a dude raped mike tyson&#039;s 10 year old granddaughter, i wouldn&#039;t contribute to the case against him because i would know that he was going to get his and it would be more fitting than the sentence that the constitutionally restricted justice system could provide him with.<br /><br />how do you feel about taking the stand and in what (if any) situations do you think it&#039;s a good idea?</div>
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext" width="85%">
							<table width="100%" border="0" style="table-layout: fixed;"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext" width="100%">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									&#171; <i>Last Edit: December 06, 2006, 11:54:20 pm by dawson</i> &#187;
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" />
									Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%; padding-bottom: 3px;" class="signature">we movin&#039; kilos by the pound...<br /><br />the views expressed in this post don&#039;t necessarily reflect the opinions of MassLine or its affiliated entities. sometimes, however, said parties are correct.</div>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
