							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=522.msg7636#msg7636"><img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=522.msg7636#msg7636">Re: the streets code..</a></b>
									<div class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #1 on:</b> December 07, 2006, 03:25:44 pm &#187;</div></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;">totally personal. what life has ttaught me is that 99% of the people out there who you think are your friends arent strong enough to hold you down when the stakes get high, and 99.9999999% of the population is gonna choose self preservation over the good of the whole when the opportunity is presented to them.<br /><br />and &quot;street code&quot;?&nbsp; cmon man, ive lived in 4 cities on two coasts and been on the docket in 3 states and i have yet to see a street code other than protect your ass. no disrespect, but maybe you need to go through the system in order to realize there is no street code outside of the movies, rap songs, and suburban fantasyland....<br /><br /></div>
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext" width="85%">
							<table width="100%" border="0" style="table-layout: fixed;"><tr>
