								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=522.msg8020#msg8020">Re: the streets code..</a></b>
									<div class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #8 on:</b> December 12, 2006, 12:09:39 am &#187;</div></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;">im kinda shocked that im reading this thread. on one hand, i see people posting about respect, community organizing, supporting each other and coming together, and then i stumble across this thread, wich smacks of &quot;stop snitching&quot;, MTV raplife drama, and suburban kids who watch &quot;the wire&quot;.<br /><br />i thought the majority of people here were above all that. maybe im missing the point, but im not so sure this thread makes any sense, and as far as i see it, anyone who has spent some significant time under state supervision will tell you that there is really rarely an opportunity to snitch or rat your buddies or be on some HBO type crime scene drama bullshit when you go into the system. the prevailing &quot;code&quot;, if you wanna call it that, is trying to roll the dice and make sure your lucky enough to cop the right PD, on the right day, and get arraigned/scentenced by the right Judge, on the right chanrge.&nbsp; (for example, some judges have personal issues with DUI&#039;s, Dom assault4&#039;s, etc.etc...)<br /><br />im not gonna go and put all my dirty laundry on the line, but i&#039;ll suffice it to say i know what the hell im talking about and on the occassions when i was locked up for an extended period of time i didnt see, hear, or give a shit about a &quot;street code&quot;, i just did what everyone else did, which was try and get a good plea and get my time over with.<br /><br />as far as wanting peoples advice on how to keep thier hands dirty OUTSIDE of the states cages, well, thats pretty much up to the individual to find out. i know one law is universal....fuck around long enough, stay dirty long enough, you&#039;ll end up on the docket SOMEWHERE, and if/when it happend, you wont be worried about street code, you&#039;ll be wondering how in the hell to get it over with....</div>
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext" width="85%">
							<table width="100%" border="0" style="table-layout: fixed;"><tr>
